<title>GERMANY: Viag shares hit high on mobile phone news.</title>
<headline>Viag shares hit high on mobile phone news.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in diversified utility Viag AG hit an all-time high in bourse trade on Tuesday after the news that the Viag-British Telekom consortium had won Germany's fourth mobile phone licence.</p>
<p>Shares were up 16.50 marks at 700.50 marks after the announcement that the German government had awarded Viag and its consortium-partner BT the licence to operate the new network. Its shares had already risen strongly in early bourse trade on anticipation of the news.</p>
<p>The overall market was up 12.17 marks, or 0.40 percent, at 3,074.46 points.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
